@title A failed import is a red triangle in the top bar with a popover; a success clears it (1920x1080)
@area Files
@sizes 1920x1080
# T12: a file that is not a DXF makes the import fail. The failure becomes a red triangle (the job flag) next to the Issues pill; a second failed job raises the count. The popover has Retry, Open folder, Copy details and Dismiss; Escape closes it; importing a real DXF clears the flag. No toast text is left on the screen.
click_text "New project"
wait 20
answer_dialog qa/fixtures/files/not-a-drawing.dxf
key ctrl+k
text import automationml
wait 5
key Enter
wait 20
shot job-flag-triangle
check_layout
expect "AML import failed"
answer_dialog qa/fixtures/files/not-a-drawing.dxf
key ctrl+k
text import dxf as background
wait 5
key Enter
wait 20
shot job-flag-count
check_layout
click_text "failed jobs" Button
wait 8
expect "Retry"
expect "Open folder"
expect "Copy details"
expect "Dismiss"
shot job-flag-popover
check_layout
key Escape
wait 6
expect_not "Copy details"
shot job-flag-popover-closed-by-escape
answer_dialog qa/fixtures/files/box.dxf
key ctrl+k
text import dxf as background
wait 5
key Enter
wait 20
expect_not "DXF import failed"
shot job-flag-cleared-by-success
check_layout
# A success clears only its own job: the AML failure is still flagged. Dismiss it and no triangle is left.
click_text "AML import failed" Button
wait 8
expect "Dismiss"
click_text "Dismiss" Button
wait 8
expect_not "AML import failed"
shot job-flag-none-left
check_layout
